      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: That is, the entire upper half of the field of view. Therefore, when the head is moved, the entire upper half of the field of view, both avatar and background, becomes jaggy.\n\nLack of anti-aliasing might be a better description. I am not familiar with this terminology and may have been inaccurate.\n\nThe phenomenon is that only during world join, the upper half of the HMD's field of view is not displayed correctly.\n\nAnd it is occurring to my friend's quest-vrchat too.\n\nI uploaded the original image and a cropped image for explanation. The image may appear to be smoothed, but it is more obvious in the HMD view.",
